Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:57:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST: Diplomacy bug fixes behind four candidate flags
 (EasyTarget, DiploBugs, LuxuryAsk, CityStateBugs)

From the Diplomacy audit (pack repo tools/ab/AUDIT.md, "Diplomacy audit"):
- EasyTarget (D1, D2): civs at peace can be rated easy targets; CP skipped
  them all because peace is war state -1. The phony-war check looks at the
  other war, not the target.
- DiploBugs: D3 phony-war peace offers can fire; D4 city-state war and bully
  targets are reset each update; D5 recent-assist sign used the right way
  round in three places; D6 full loyalty weight for defending a friend from
  a weak attacker; D7 land dispute re-evaluates when it rises; D8 units near
  another war aren't counted as aggressive posture; D12 the World Congress
  AI compares resolution types when halving a repeat proposal; D13 a refused
  help request starts a shorter wait (no same-turn re-roll).
- LuxuryAsk (D9): when balancing a deal the AI can ask for the other
  side's luxuries (CP only listed them for import-monopoly civs).
- CityStateBugs (D10, D11): a city-state's alliance passes to a civ that
  overtook the ally; city-states roll separately on joining a war against
  an aggressor. Game-wide: on when any major civ has the flag.

All four are left out of the bundle (kCandidateFixBundle) until tested.

